  "evidenceBoundary": {
    "exact": "Selected .pdata body extents, full body hashes, instruction bytes, managed metadata identity/staticness/full runtime parameter and return signatures/registered pointer and 64-byte method windows. Full regular/external parameter counts, ordered names and registered runtime types are proved; selected enum value__ instance fields establish signed 32-bit callbackType and unsigned 32-bit codec storage.",
    "direct": "SetSource memory/info overloads copy 16 bytes through the aggregate pointer into source+0, OR source+12 with 0x80, store the unsigned scalar at source+24, and memory overload stores the pointer at source+16. Scalar-only overload writes the scalar to source+0 and resets fields. LockDataPtr reads source+12 bit 8: clear passes source+0 to registry lookup; set forwards source+16 pointer and source+8 count into the output reference. Helpers write output pointers at +0/+8/+16 and byte count at +24. The registry implementation has early returns that can retain the incoming output reference; a post-call observation is not by itself a successful lookup.",
    "structuralOnly": "Info/source words retain anonymous names except directly observed lookup, flags, pointer, and output-count roles. Historical SDK labels are provenance, not a current SDK type-layout proof. The info capture span is the 16-byte copied input region, not a proof of an independently recovered complete C++ type layout.",
    "conditional": "A complete same-thread SetSource call/result followed by LockDataPtr on the same source pointer, with no intervening captured SetSource on it, can witness local source-to-output-pointer state. Reused pointer addresses, asynchronous managed-to-native work, and uncaptured resets require additional lifetime evidence.",
    "unresolved": "External key/cookie to source lookup word, backing file identity, codec-family selection, decoded content, execution success, and audibility are not proved by this profile."
  },
